# Juno AI Computer Use Agent - Project Essentials ✅

## Project Overview

**Juno** is a **COMPLETE** Tauri v2 desktop application implementing Anthropic's Computer Use API with hierarchical agent architecture, advanced voice transcription capabilities, and **production-ready cloud control system**. The project represents a production-ready AI computer use agent with enhanced capabilities beyond the official specification.

## Implementation Status: ✅ PRODUCTION READY

## Tech Stack
- **Frontend**: React/TypeScript with shadcn/ui components
- **Backend**: Rust with Tauri v2 framework
- **AI Integration**: Multi-provider support (Anthropic, OpenAI, Gemini)
- **Voice**: Custom Whisper.cpp-based transcription plugin
- **Platform**: macOS with native automation APIs
- **Cloud**: WebSocket-based remote control with security layer

### Core Features (100% Complete)
- **✅ Official Anthropic Computer Use Tools**: All 17 actions implemented (screenshot, mouse, keyboard, scroll, wait)
- **✅ Enhanced File Operations**: Complete str_replace_based_edit_tool with view, create, edit, insert capabilities
- **✅ Shell Command Execution**: bash_20250124 with output capture and session management
- **✅ Advanced Voice System**: Dual-mode voice interaction (Agent + Dictation)
- **✅ Hierarchical Agent Architecture**: Orchestrator with specialist agents (browser, desktop, file)
- **✅ Timer System**: Long-running task management with screen/file/app monitoring
- **✅ MCP Integration**: External tool server support with protocol compliance

### Recent Updates (January 2025) ✅
- **MCP Protocol Compliance**: Fixed initialization errors, now fully compliant with MCP 2025-03-26 spec
- **Simplified UI Configuration**: JSON-only MCP server configuration with examples
- **Protocol Error Resolution**: Resolved "protocolVersion and clientInfo required" issues
- **Enhanced Tool Integration**: Seamless local + external tool execution

